{
  "name": "twitter-binding-pages-past-1000",
  "description": "TwitterFlow's twitter:search only passes query/since/until, so every page returns the same 100 tweets: 11 binding calls (1100 > 1000) set moreTweets, the list is cut to 1000, and only the last occurrence of each tweet id receives a sentiment (idToTweet map); unclassified tweets count as positive.",
  "source": {
    "muleApp": "mule-component-bindings",
    "flow": "StockServiceFlow",
    "evidence": "documented",
    "reference": "mule-component-bindings/src/main/java/stockstats/impl/StockStatsResourceImpl.java (paging loop, maxResults 1000); mule-component-bindings/src/main/app/mule-component-bindings.xml (TwitterFlow twitter:search query/since/until); mule-component-bindings/src/main/java/stockstats/impl/mule/TwitterRequestProcessor.java (until = date + 10d); mule-component-bindings/src/main/java/stockstats/impl/sentiment140/Sentiment140SentimentService.java; stockstats/SocialStats.java"
  },
